{
  "sampleRate": 22050,
  "version": "v2",
  "notes": "Domino droid voice v2 (2026-11-15): v1 plus a spoken voice and a post pass. The owner's favourites (whistle, cuckoo, purr) work because they copy sounds a mouth makes, so v2 gives the droid a mouth: wave 'vox' sings a vowel (vowel: oo | oh | ah | uh | eh | ee | mm, or 'oo>ah' to glide between two), and each emote is a small spoken gesture (hello, uh-oh, hmm?, aww, wow) with a quiet whistle on top. fx is the post pass applied to every sound: drive = soft distortion (1 = none), echoMs/echoGain and echo2Ms/echo2Gain = two short echoes, lowpassHz = treble roll-off. v1 is frozen in sounds/wav/v1. Segment fields: wave: sine | tri | sq | fm | hop | vox. f0->f1 is a glide in Hz over ms, then gap ms of silence. curve: lin | exp. vib/vibDepth: vibrato rate (Hz) and depth. sub: 0..1 mix of a second sine voice at subRatio times the pitch (0.5 = octave down, 2 = whistle an octave up). atk/rel: fade in/out in ms. amp 0..1. phrases string emotes together (name, pause in ms, or {emote, pitch, tempo}). babble makes a long seeded sentence at build time. Edit, then run: node sounds/build.mjs",
  "fx": {
